ems in.",[152,156,157,161],{},[158,159,160],"strong",{},"Ports list → Add"," lists the serial ports of the computer that are not in use yet. System ports\n(Bluetooth, debug consoles) are hidden.",[152,163,164,165,168,169,172],{},"Tick the ports and press ",[158,166,167],{},"Add",", or ",[158,170,171],{},"Add all ports",".",[134,174,175,176,179],{},"Added ports are remembered: the gateway reconnects them on every start and whenever a modem is\nplugged back into the same USB port. ",[158,177,178],{},"Remove from worked"," forgets a port.",[134,181,182,183,187,188,191,192,194,195,172],{},"Network serial bridges (",[184,185,186],"code",{},"tcp:\u002F\u002Fhost:port",") and Bluetooth LE UART adapters (",[184,189,190],{},"ble:\u002F\u002F…",") are added on the\n",[158,193,109],{}," page and then appear in the same list. See ",[196,197,78],"a",{"href":79},[144,199,201],{"id":200},"the-port-list","The port list",[134,203,204],{},"Each row shows the port, the operator, the number, the signal and a status. The filter above the list\nnarrows it to available, worked, online or problem ports. Select a row to open the detail panel:\nname and number of the port, SIM data (IMSI, ICCID, IMEI, operator, country), income, and the\nservices that used or banned the number.",[206,207,208,221],"table",{},[209,210,211],"thead",{},[212,213,214,218],"tr",{},[215,216,217],"th",{},"Status",[215,219,220],{},"Meaning",[222,223,224,235,245,255,265,275],"tbody",{},[212,225,226,232],{},[227,228,229],"td",{},[158,230,231],{},"Online",[227,233,234],{},"The number is on sale.",[212,236,237,242],{},[227,238,239],{},[158,240,241],{},"Queued",[227,243,244],{},"The number was sent to the server and waits to go on sale.",[212,246,247,252],{},[227,248,249],{},[158,250,251],{},"Connecting",[227,253,254],{},"The gateway is talking to the modem or the server right now.",[212,256,257,262],{},[227,258,259],{},[158,260,261],{},"Offline",[227,263,264],{},"The modem works but the number is not on sale (auto-connect off, not logged in).",[212,266,267,272],{},[227,268,269],{},[158,270,271],{},"Issue",[227,273,274],{},"Something needs attention: the banner in the detail panel says what.",[212,276,277,282],{},[227,278,279],{},[158,280,281],{},"Disconnected",[227,283,284],{},"The modem is not plugged in or does not answer.",[144,286,288],{"id":287},"port-actions","Port actions",[134,290,291],{},"Right-click a port (or use the buttons of the detail panel):",[293,294,295,301,307,313,319,325],"ul",{},[152,296,297,300],{},[158,298,299],{},"SMS inbox"," — messages the SIM received.",[152,302,303,306],{},[158,304,305],{},"LED notification"," — blinks the modem, to find it in a rack.",[152,308,309,312],{},[158,310,311],{},"Reset errors and reconnect"," — clears the errors and lists the number again; also puts a port\nwith a known number on sale without the global auto-connect.",[152,314,315,318],{},[158,316,317],{},"Clear number"," — takes the number off sale and forgets it (a new SIM, a changed number).",[152,320,321,324],{},[158,322,323],{},"Show error"," — the full text of the last error.",[152,326,327,329],{},[158,328,178],{}," — forget the port.",[134,331,332,333,336],{},"The toolbar above the list sends USSD to many ports at once (",[158,334,335],{},"More → Bulk USSD",") and checks the\nhealth of every modem.",{"title":338,"searchDepth":339,"depth":339,"links":340},"",2,[341,342,343],{"id":146,"depth":339,"text":147},{"id":200,"depth":339,"text":201},{"id":287,"depth":339,"text":288},"Adding ports, reading the port list and what each status means.","md",null,{},{"icon":24},{"title":21,"description":344},"mjg4rZ5-txs-YRmIE9QQuBx_HiD8KM91Ux5H6fUJbYs",[352,354],{"title":16,"path":17,"description":353},"Installers for Windows, macOS and Linux, which file to pick and where the gateway keeps its data.",{"title":26,"path":27,"description":355},"How a SIM becomes a number on sale, auto-connect, rent, and what the server's answers mean.",1794978318119]